[h2]Fixed: red uber monsters that dropped no loot orb[/h2]

[b]A player report, and the audit it triggered.[/b] The Boar Snatcher - the red legendary spider in the Greek pine forest and the Spartan optional cave - died without dropping a Mystical Orb, while the other red uber monsters all drop one. He does now.

[list]
[*][b]The Boar Snatcher drops a Mystical Orb.[/b] All three of his level variants were wired to the same generic boss orb the other low-level red ubers pay out. He is a base-game monster the mod had never touched, which is exactly why he slipped through: every drop audit this mod had ever run looked only at records the mod itself owns, and he is not one of them.
[*][b]Seven more red ubers were silently orb-less, and are now fixed too.[/b] Once the audit was widened to the real runtime world - the mod plus the base game together - it found 55 red uber monsters, of which 14 paid no orb. Neferkha, the frost uber, the higher Phagia, Aithon in the Olympian Arena and Kravmoloch all now drop an orb matched to their level band. Six more are deliberate exceptions and were proven to be so: four are transformation shells whose final form already carries the orb, and two are summoned copies that are not supposed to drop anything at all.
[*][b]A permanent gate so this class of bug cannot come back.[/b] Every orb in this mod used to be attached by a hand-typed list, which is how monsters got missed. The build now derives the whole red uber roster from the data and fails loudly if any red uber ships without an orb, with each exception having to re-prove itself every build.
[/list]

[i]No drop rate was lowered and no existing chest, orb or loot table was changed - this update only adds orbs to monsters that had none. The Spartan Crypt entrance fix and the chest breadth work from the previous update are included.[/i]

